### Part 4: Step-by-Step GitHub Setup Guide

#### 1. Push Files to GitHub
If you prefer doing it entirely inside the web browser:
1. Go to your new GitHub Repository on github.com.
2. Click **uploading an existing file** or create a new file.
3. Create **`index.html`** and paste the code from **Part 2**.
4. Create **`README.md`** and paste the code from **Part 3**.
5. Commit the changes directly to your `main` branch.

#### 2. Enable GitHub Pages (To Host the Live App)
1. In your GitHub repository, click on the **Settings** tab.
2. Under the left-hand sidebar, look for **Pages** (under the Code and automation section).
3. Under **Build and deployment** > **Branch**, select **`main`** (or your primary branch) and directory **`/ (root)`**.
4. Click **Save**.
5. After a minute, your app will be hosted live on your custom GitHub Pages address:  
   `https://YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME.github.io/Expense-Tracker/`

Once your GitHub Pages link is live, copy it and paste it into the primary download/visit buttons inside your portfolio blog post.
